1
00:00:07,897 --> 00:00:10,027
(Space Rice Cake)

2
00:00:10,157 --> 00:00:13,167
(Just another ordinary commute)

3
00:00:13,427 --> 00:00:15,397
(A guest was already there for a surprise appearance.)

4
00:00:15,597 --> 00:00:18,137
(Doh Kyung Soo, the seasoned part-timer)

5
00:00:18,307 --> 00:00:19,307
(No, that's not right.)

6
00:00:19,307 --> 00:00:20,807
(Like this...)

7
00:00:21,107 --> 00:00:23,137
(Under the strict director's supervision,)

8
00:00:23,337 --> 00:00:26,477
(they sweated buckets learning to make a new dish.)

9
00:00:26,647 --> 00:00:28,877
(Rice cracker taco)

10
00:00:28,877 --> 00:00:31,787
(The perfect director's sweet and caring side...)

11
00:00:31,947 --> 00:00:34,087
(made them smile despite the exhaustion.)

12
00:00:34,217 --> 00:00:36,757
(He was leading the team smoothly.)

13
00:00:36,927 --> 00:00:40,757
(But once he started serving customers,)

14
00:00:40,857 --> 00:00:43,897
(his cool director charisma vanished.)

15
00:00:43,967 --> 00:00:44,967
(The shrimp burger is included, right?)

16
00:00:46,397 --> 00:00:48,567
(He turned into a nervous wreck, just like a rookie part-timer.)

17
00:00:48,897 --> 00:00:50,337
(When will you start making the taco?)

18
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:51,967
(We'll start as soon as an order comes in.)

19
00:00:52,107 --> 00:00:53,407
(I think I left it off the order.)

20
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:54,577
Did they order it?

21
00:00:55,007 --> 00:00:57,947
(They're working with the part-timer who keeps making mistakes.)

22
00:01:02,817 --> 00:01:05,517
(Did you seek out hardships?)

23
00:01:05,747 --> 00:01:06,747
- Mi Hyun. - Yes?

24
00:01:06,747 --> 00:01:08,117
This one is way too dark. What should we do?

25
00:01:08,117 --> 00:01:09,517
I only fried it for a minute.

26
00:01:09,917 --> 00:01:11,887
- It was in the fryer for a minute? - Yes, the oil was at 200°C.

27
00:01:11,887 --> 00:01:13,327
No, you shouldn't set the temperature to 200°C.

28
00:01:13,897 --> 00:01:15,597
It shouldn't be at 200°C. Let's fry a new one.

29
00:01:16,527 --> 00:01:17,867
- Let's start over again. - Hold on.

30
00:01:19,097 --> 00:01:20,537
We shouldn't fry it at 200°C, right?

31
00:01:20,537 --> 00:01:22,437
That's right. The temperature is perfect now.

32
00:01:22,997 --> 00:01:24,907
- Young Ji, I put it in the fryer. - Okay.

33
00:01:25,407 --> 00:01:27,007
(Tension fills the kitchen.)

34
00:01:27,007 --> 00:01:28,907
- You can check it later. - Okay.

35
00:01:29,577 --> 00:01:31,677
(Yu Jin is prepping pizza.)

36
00:01:32,247 --> 00:01:33,877
This is a disaster.

37
00:01:34,547 --> 00:01:35,917
It's because it's bigger than the tray.

38
00:01:35,917 --> 00:01:38,087
But with the powder, it doesn't stick here.

39
00:01:38,087 --> 00:01:39,787
(The patty is burnt.)

40
00:01:39,787 --> 00:01:40,917
It's okay. How...

41
00:01:40,917 --> 00:01:42,587
What should we do about this?

42
00:01:42,717 --> 00:01:43,987
Should we cut it?

43
00:01:44,157 --> 00:01:45,357
- Rather than keep that part. - You think so?

44
00:01:45,627 --> 00:01:47,027
(Pure chaos in the kitchen)

45
00:01:47,457 --> 00:01:48,957
(Screaming and chatting)

46
00:01:49,427 --> 00:01:50,567
A new group of customers is here.

47
00:01:50,567 --> 00:01:51,567
(In the middle of the chaos, new customers arrive.)

48
00:01:51,867 --> 00:01:53,297
May I take your name, please?

49
00:01:53,297 --> 00:01:54,737
(She has to take their order too.)

50
00:01:54,737 --> 00:01:56,267
- Yes. - Can we have one shrimp burger...

51
00:01:56,267 --> 00:01:58,067
- Yes. - and one taco, please?

52
00:01:58,067 --> 00:01:59,067
- Of course. - And...

53
00:01:59,067 --> 00:02:00,907
- one cake, please. - Sure.

54
00:02:01,237 --> 00:02:03,007
Can we also have one glass of pomegranate ade...

55
00:02:03,007 --> 00:02:04,247
- and two glasses of yuzu ade? - Okay.

56
00:02:04,247 --> 00:02:05,747
- I'll give you the receipt. - One shrimp burger...

57
00:02:05,747 --> 00:02:07,317
(But...)

58
00:02:07,617 --> 00:02:08,677
I'm sorry, ma'am.

59
00:02:08,677 --> 00:02:10,647
- I'll redo the payment for you. - Okay.

60
00:02:10,647 --> 00:02:13,087
- I'll add one glass of yuzu ade. - Okay.

61
00:02:13,217 --> 00:02:15,317
(She redoes the payment.)

62
00:02:15,317 --> 00:02:16,457
- Yes. - We're ready to order.

63
00:02:16,457 --> 00:02:17,457
All right.

64
00:02:17,457 --> 00:02:18,657
(Drink Order: 1 pomegranate ade, 2 yuzu ades)

65
00:02:18,657 --> 00:02:21,227
(A total of 3 glasses)

66
00:02:21,227 --> 00:02:23,427
My mind was all over the place. This one has been served.

67
00:02:23,427 --> 00:02:24,527
(But, on the ticket...)

68
00:02:24,527 --> 00:02:25,527
(Drink Order: Pomegranate ade included in the combo)

69
00:02:25,527 --> 00:02:28,197
(One more glass of yuzu ade?)

70
00:02:28,467 --> 00:02:30,197
The drinks that are ready...

71
00:02:30,197 --> 00:02:31,967
- Thanks. Should we serve them? - Yes.

72
00:02:31,967 --> 00:02:33,537
- Let's just serve them first. - Okay. I'll be right back.

73
00:02:33,537 --> 00:02:34,677
- Before the ice melts. - Okay.

74
00:02:34,807 --> 00:02:36,137
- Table Seven. I'll be right back. - Yes.

75
00:02:36,707 --> 00:02:38,447
Yes, I'm carrying the drinks.

76
00:02:38,447 --> 00:02:40,307
- Thank you. - Don't mention it.

77
00:02:45,517 --> 00:02:47,057
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

78
00:02:47,257 --> 00:02:50,117
Eun Ji, when will our ades be served?

79
00:02:50,117 --> 00:02:51,727
- What dishes did you order? - I meant the ades.

80
00:02:51,727 --> 00:02:53,127
- Right. I'll bring them right over. - One of them is pomegranate ade.

81
00:02:53,127 --> 00:02:55,397
I'm very sorry. These are for that table.

82
00:02:55,397 --> 00:02:56,397
Really?

83
00:02:56,397 --> 00:02:57,567
That's okay. No problem.

84
00:02:57,567 --> 00:02:58,597
That was a close call.

85
00:02:58,597 --> 00:03:00,027
- They're for us, right? - Thank you for pointing that out.

86
00:03:00,097 --> 00:03:01,637
- Thank you so much. - They're for Table Seven.

87
00:03:01,637 --> 00:03:03,437
- Yes... - Because we came first.

88
00:03:03,437 --> 00:03:05,567
Exactly. I totally understand.

89
00:03:05,567 --> 00:03:07,537
- Please help me out for a second. - Okay.

90
00:03:07,537 --> 00:03:09,777
You ordered one shrimp burger, right?

91
00:03:09,777 --> 00:03:11,277
- Yes. - How much is it?

92
00:03:11,947 --> 00:03:12,947
Right here...

93
00:03:12,947 --> 00:03:15,677
(They're huddled up like a study group.)

94
00:03:15,847 --> 00:03:18,087
Could I just cancel everything...

95
00:03:18,087 --> 00:03:19,847
- and redo the payment? - Sure.

96
00:03:19,847 --> 00:03:20,857
- Got it. - That'll be no problem.

97
00:03:21,187 --> 00:03:23,157
- If you give me your credit card... - Did we order tacos too?

98
00:03:23,687 --> 00:03:24,827
Taco? Oh, right.

99
00:03:24,927 --> 00:03:26,957
We ordered one taco as well.

100
00:03:26,957 --> 00:03:28,027
Okay.

101
00:03:28,027 --> 00:03:29,427
You didn't order any tacos...

102
00:03:30,227 --> 00:03:32,767
(Yes, they did.)

103
00:03:33,097 --> 00:03:34,397
- Yes, we did. - Yes.

104
00:03:34,397 --> 00:03:36,037
- Did you order tacos? - Yes.

105
00:03:36,037 --> 00:03:37,907
(The more they analyze the order, the more confused they get.)

106
00:03:38,107 --> 00:03:39,907
All together, your total comes to...

107
00:03:40,267 --> 00:03:42,277
I'll tell you when you go home.

108
00:03:42,277 --> 00:03:43,377
- Okay. I understand. - Okay.

109
00:03:43,377 --> 00:03:44,807
- I'll be back with your food. - Okay.

110
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:46,377
- Thank you. - Thank you.

111
00:03:46,377 --> 00:03:48,247
(Their study group session is over, but they're left with homework.)

112
00:03:48,617 --> 00:03:50,647
Is anything confusing you?

113
00:03:50,647 --> 00:03:51,887
- Yes, this one. - Right.

114
00:03:52,047 --> 00:03:53,757
- I messed up the order. - Are we down one yuzu ade?

115
00:03:53,757 --> 00:03:55,187
But I took care of it.

116
00:03:55,357 --> 00:03:57,087
One carrot... Oh, we got one taco for this order.

117
00:03:57,087 --> 00:03:59,187
- Was it on the ticket? - No, there was no taco on it.

118
00:03:59,187 --> 00:04:01,127
- Let me clear this up. - Okay.

119
00:04:01,727 --> 00:04:03,897
Mi Hyun, I took the order incorrectly earlier.

120
00:04:03,897 --> 00:04:05,467
- Please make one taco. - Sure.

121
00:04:05,467 --> 00:04:06,567
Thank you.

122
00:04:06,827 --> 00:04:08,097
- Kyung Soo. - Yes?

123
00:04:08,097 --> 00:04:10,297
Can you make two glasses of pomegranate ade...

124
00:04:10,297 --> 00:04:11,467
and one glass of yuzu ade for me?

125
00:04:11,467 --> 00:04:13,237
- I'm working on it right now. - Okay.

126
00:04:13,807 --> 00:04:15,007
We have perfect teamwork.

127
00:04:15,837 --> 00:04:18,607
Today, I feel like we've finally hit our stride.

128
00:04:19,247 --> 00:04:20,617
(She's calmly making a shrimp burger.)

129
00:04:20,617 --> 00:04:22,377
One shrimp burger is up.

130
00:04:22,817 --> 00:04:23,817
Okay.

131
00:04:24,087 --> 00:04:26,117
One more taco is ready.

132
00:04:26,117 --> 00:04:27,117
Got it.

133
00:04:27,957 --> 00:04:29,557
The carrot cake and taco.

134
00:04:30,157 --> 00:04:31,187
It's perfect.

135
00:04:31,187 --> 00:04:32,287
(Table 8: 1 shrimp burger combo, 1 taco, 1 carrot cake)

136
00:04:32,557 --> 00:04:35,757
(The part-timer made 3 glasses of ade skillfully.)

137
00:04:35,757 --> 00:04:37,327
These are all for Table Eight.

138
00:04:37,327 --> 00:04:39,027
- I'll serve them to Table Eight. - A shrimp burger, a carrot cake...

139
00:04:39,027 --> 00:04:40,097
(The dishes have been made in an instant.)

140
00:04:40,297 --> 00:04:41,337
Hello.

141
00:04:41,337 --> 00:04:42,837
(The food is served instantly to minimize the wait.)

142
00:04:42,997 --> 00:04:44,307
- Thank you. - Here's your food.

143
00:04:44,307 --> 00:04:45,707
(Table 8: Everything has been served.)

144
00:04:45,707 --> 00:04:46,707
Here's the taco.

145
00:04:46,707 --> 00:04:48,437
- Here's your pizza. - Our food is here.

146
00:04:48,537 --> 00:04:49,577
Oh, great.

147
00:04:49,777 --> 00:04:52,147
- Here you go. - Thank you.

148
00:04:52,347 --> 00:04:55,077
(Every dish has been served!)

149
00:04:55,347 --> 00:04:59,187
(She's pausing for a quick breather.)

150
00:04:59,687 --> 00:05:01,417
(We're waiting for customers)

151
00:05:01,417 --> 00:05:03,257
(Maru sniffs, Maru perks up)

152
00:05:03,257 --> 00:05:04,557
(Maru snatches)

153
00:05:04,827 --> 00:05:06,587
(Maru zooms and zooms)

154
00:05:06,687 --> 00:05:09,327
(Our little puppy is waiting for customers.)

155
00:05:09,327 --> 00:05:12,797
(Walking)

156
00:05:13,327 --> 00:05:18,267
(The long-awaited party of 4 arrives.)

157
00:05:18,507 --> 00:05:19,667
(But then...)

158
00:05:22,377 --> 00:05:26,477
(Another party of 4 walks in.)

159
00:05:26,847 --> 00:05:30,917
(All 8 customers arrive at the same time.)

160
00:05:31,187 --> 00:05:32,687
- I'll serve the food. - Okay.

161
00:05:32,687 --> 00:05:34,217
- Welcome. - Hello.

162
00:05:34,217 --> 00:05:35,287
Hello.

163
00:05:36,587 --> 00:05:37,657
He's fast.

164
00:05:37,657 --> 00:05:38,687
(Oh, my. He's fast.)

165
00:05:38,787 --> 00:05:40,897
He was moving at supersonic speed just now.

166
00:05:41,297 --> 00:05:43,597
- We got a new order. - Yes, sir.

167
00:05:44,527 --> 00:05:46,567
One pizza, one taco,

168
00:05:46,697 --> 00:05:48,737
one carrot cake, and one beef burger.

169
00:05:49,097 --> 00:05:50,907
One pizza, one taco,

170
00:05:50,907 --> 00:05:52,707
one shrimp burger, and one beef burger.

171
00:05:52,707 --> 00:05:53,707
- Got it. - Got it.

172
00:05:53,767 --> 00:05:54,837
One pizza.

173
00:05:54,837 --> 00:05:55,907
- One pizza and one taco. - One pizza.

174
00:05:56,107 --> 00:05:57,107
Okay.

175
00:05:57,107 --> 00:05:58,547
(Oiling the pan to get ready for the taco)

176
00:05:58,707 --> 00:06:00,717
(In goes a big ladleful of minced meat.)

177
00:06:01,047 --> 00:06:03,517
(Infusing the meat with the rich aroma of garlic)

178
00:06:03,777 --> 00:06:06,187
(Next, adding the taco seasoning, the key to the whole flavor)

179
00:06:06,447 --> 00:06:09,087
(Stir-frying everything until the flavors are perfectly combined)

180
00:06:09,357 --> 00:06:10,987
(Topped with refreshing tomato salsa...)

181
00:06:11,357 --> 00:06:13,287
(and savory avocados)

182
00:06:13,627 --> 00:06:14,957
I'll take it out, Mi Hyun.

183
00:06:15,197 --> 00:06:16,227
Okay.

184
00:06:16,227 --> 00:06:19,227
(Squeezing on a generous amount of sour cream)

185
00:06:19,867 --> 00:06:21,697
One taco is ready.

186
00:06:21,697 --> 00:06:22,967
(As Mimi wraps up the taco,)

187
00:06:23,237 --> 00:06:24,437
(her partner Young Ji starts prepping the beef burger.)

188
00:06:24,437 --> 00:06:26,137
I want them to eat it while it's warm.

189
00:06:26,637 --> 00:06:29,477
(And she fries a shrimp patty...)

190
00:06:29,477 --> 00:06:31,947
(and tater tots perfectly.)

191
00:06:32,277 --> 00:06:35,277
(Their positions are switched, but their professional mode stays on.)

192
00:06:35,747 --> 00:06:36,747
Okay.

193
00:06:36,747 --> 00:06:38,587
(Meanwhile, Yu Jin plates the pizza.)

194
00:06:38,747 --> 00:06:40,617
Yu Jin, if you're busy, I'll do it.

195
00:06:40,617 --> 00:06:42,457
- I'm fine for now. - Okay.

196
00:06:42,457 --> 00:06:43,957
Yu Jin, I'll serve the cake.

197
00:06:43,957 --> 00:06:45,057
Thank you.

198
00:06:45,457 --> 00:06:47,457
Then I should make the ade, right?

199
00:06:48,297 --> 00:06:52,167
(The service team has great teamwork.)

200
00:06:52,627 --> 00:06:57,767
(The part-timer makes the ade skillfully.)

201
00:06:57,967 --> 00:07:00,737
(Right then, a group of customers leaves.)

202
00:07:00,977 --> 00:07:04,547
(Once the customers leave,)

203
00:07:04,747 --> 00:07:07,947
(the next mission awaits.)

204
00:07:07,947 --> 00:07:08,977
Kyung Soo,

205
00:07:08,977 --> 00:07:11,047
please go upstairs and clear the table.

206
00:07:11,187 --> 00:07:15,617
(While Kyung Soo cheerfully clears the table...)

207
00:07:15,787 --> 00:07:17,527
One taco is ready.

208
00:07:17,687 --> 00:07:19,327
The pizza is ready.

209
00:07:19,457 --> 00:07:23,327
(After they serve food busily...)

210
00:07:24,367 --> 00:07:25,527
Goodness. This is exhausting.

211
00:07:25,527 --> 00:07:27,267
(Empty plates start coming out.)

212
00:07:27,697 --> 00:07:31,167
(The service team takes turns doing the dishes.)

213
00:07:31,337 --> 00:07:32,907
You served the pizza earlier...

214
00:07:32,907 --> 00:07:34,037
We should cross this one off.

215
00:07:34,277 --> 00:07:35,277
We should cross this one off too.

216
00:07:35,277 --> 00:07:36,277
- This one is out. - Is it out?

217
00:07:36,277 --> 00:07:37,277
It's out.

218
00:07:37,277 --> 00:07:39,447
But the drinks aren't ready yet.

219
00:07:39,447 --> 00:07:40,817
(They didn't have time to make the ades.)

220
00:07:40,817 --> 00:07:43,247
If you make two glasses each of pomegranate and yuzu ade,

221
00:07:43,247 --> 00:07:44,617
- I'll serve them on this tray. - Okay.

222
00:07:45,017 --> 00:07:46,747
- Two pomegranate and two yuzu. - You're so smart.

223
00:07:47,957 --> 00:07:49,887
Two yuzu and one pomegranate, Yu Jin?

224
00:07:49,887 --> 00:07:51,927
- Two of each. - Okay.

225
00:07:52,227 --> 00:07:53,757
Thank you, Yu Jin.

226
00:07:53,757 --> 00:07:55,227
- Don't mention it. - Oh, gosh.

227
00:07:55,557 --> 00:07:58,927
(The ade, as refreshing as Yu Jin, is ready.)

228
00:07:59,367 --> 00:08:00,997
I'm going to serve one carrot cake too.

229
00:08:00,997 --> 00:08:02,097
(Following the drinks, the carrot cake is ready too.)

230
00:08:02,567 --> 00:08:04,307
- These are for Table Ten. - Eun Ji, this is for...

231
00:08:04,307 --> 00:08:05,367
(Table 10: 1 mint carrot cake, 2 pomegranate ades, 2 yuzu ades)

232
00:08:05,367 --> 00:08:06,367
One carrot cake.

233
00:08:10,137 --> 00:08:11,147
Thank you so much.

234
00:08:12,107 --> 00:08:14,777
(So she arrived at the destination?)

235
00:08:16,747 --> 00:08:18,887
Please stir it well before you drink it.

236
00:08:18,887 --> 00:08:20,757
- Okay. - Thank you.

237
00:08:20,757 --> 00:08:22,057
- Thank you. - Thank you.

238
00:08:22,057 --> 00:08:23,557
(The ades have been served to the wrong table.)

239
00:08:23,857 --> 00:08:25,387
(Actually...)

240
00:08:25,487 --> 00:08:28,557
(We're Table 10.)

241
00:08:28,927 --> 00:08:31,197
- You ordered a carrot cake, right? - Yes.

242
00:08:31,197 --> 00:08:32,597
- Thank you. - Here you go. Thank you.

243
00:08:32,597 --> 00:08:33,667
(Fortunately, she served the cake to the right table.)

244
00:08:33,997 --> 00:08:37,097
(Table 10: 1 mint carrot cake)

245
00:08:37,407 --> 00:08:40,137
(Meanwhile, Yu Jin fills the next tray.)

246
00:08:40,437 --> 00:08:43,837
(Table 11: 1 mint carrot cake, 2 pomegranate ades, 2 yuzu ades)

247
00:08:44,077 --> 00:08:46,947
(It's the exact same menu combination.)

248
00:08:47,417 --> 00:08:49,577
- Kyung Soo, can you go to Table 11? - Sure.

249
00:08:49,847 --> 00:08:51,147
These are all for Table 11.

250
00:08:51,717 --> 00:08:53,647
- Table 11? - Yes, they're all for Table 11.

251
00:08:54,487 --> 00:08:58,387
(Table 11)

252
00:08:59,187 --> 00:09:01,527
(Pausing)

253
00:09:06,927 --> 00:09:10,167
(They already have their ades.)

254
00:09:10,637 --> 00:09:14,207
(The part-timer is holding a tray fully loaded with ades.)

255
00:09:14,937 --> 00:09:18,177
(Stepping backward)

256
00:09:19,077 --> 00:09:20,147
- These aren't for Table 11. - What's going on?

257
00:09:20,747 --> 00:09:23,117
- They're not for Table 11? - They already have their drinks.

258
00:09:23,117 --> 00:09:25,717
If they're not for Table 11, which table ordered them?

259
00:09:26,117 --> 00:09:28,417
- Is everything okay? - Yes.

260
00:09:28,417 --> 00:09:29,517
(Yu Jin heard the news and stepped in.)

261
00:09:29,817 --> 00:09:32,587
(She searches the dining area aimlessly.)

262
00:09:33,127 --> 00:09:34,827
Is everything okay?

263
00:09:34,827 --> 00:09:36,397
Yes, everything is very delicious.

264
00:09:36,557 --> 00:09:38,767
Is there anything you need?

265
00:09:39,067 --> 00:09:40,797
Has anything you ordered not been served?

266
00:09:41,797 --> 00:09:42,897
- We're good. - We're good.

267
00:09:43,397 --> 00:09:44,467
She's cute.

268
00:09:44,467 --> 00:09:46,767
(The ades have nowhere to go.)

269
00:09:47,137 --> 00:09:48,207
If they're not for Table 11, then where?

270
00:09:48,207 --> 00:09:50,507
(The service team is confused.)

271
00:09:50,607 --> 00:09:52,677
- Table 11 got everything. - Table 10 and 11.

272
00:09:52,777 --> 00:09:54,477
I'll check with Table 10. You go check with Table 11.

273
00:09:54,977 --> 00:09:57,377
I think I gave you the wrong table number. I'm sorry, Kyung Soo.

274
00:09:58,547 --> 00:10:01,487
(Puppy goes on her second round of patrol.)

275
00:10:03,987 --> 00:10:05,957
- You didn't get your ades, did you? - No, we didn't.

276
00:10:06,357 --> 00:10:09,057
- We found them! - We have your ades right here.

277
00:10:09,057 --> 00:10:11,427
(Here are your ades.)

278
00:10:11,767 --> 00:10:12,797
We found them!

279
00:10:12,797 --> 00:10:13,827
(They're finally served to the right table.)

280
00:10:13,867 --> 00:10:14,937
(Table 10: 2 pomegranate ades, 2 yuzu ades)

281
00:10:14,937 --> 00:10:15,997
(Table 10: Everything has been served.)

282
00:10:16,037 --> 00:10:19,067
- Doh Kyung Soo! - Doh Kyung Soo!

283
00:10:19,307 --> 00:10:20,467
(They're chanting the part-timer's name for some unknown reason.)

284
00:10:20,467 --> 00:10:22,177
- Here's your ade. - Doh Kyung Soo!

285
00:10:22,177 --> 00:10:23,937
Did you order two of these?

286
00:10:23,937 --> 00:10:25,607
- No, we ordered just one. - No.

287
00:10:25,707 --> 00:10:27,517
(Their carrot cake has already been served.)

288
00:10:27,617 --> 00:10:30,347
- You ordered just 1? Okay. - I think it's for Table 11.

289
00:10:30,517 --> 00:10:32,847
Table 11, has your carrot cake been served?

290
00:10:32,847 --> 00:10:34,017
- No, it hasn't. - The carrot cake...

291
00:10:34,157 --> 00:10:35,357
(They found the customers who ordered the carrot cake.)

292
00:10:35,657 --> 00:10:37,387
(Table 11: 1 mint carrot cake)

293
00:10:37,387 --> 00:10:40,357
(Shout "Doh Kyung Soo" when you're happy.)

294
00:10:40,657 --> 00:10:43,557
- Doh Kyung Soo! - Please enjoy.

295
00:10:44,057 --> 00:10:46,167
That went well. That was great.

296
00:10:46,867 --> 00:10:48,097
(This is fun.)

297
00:10:48,097 --> 00:10:49,197
(This is really fun.)

298
00:10:49,437 --> 00:10:52,407
(They return with light hearts.)

299
00:10:52,867 --> 00:10:54,007
It's totally over.

300
00:10:54,777 --> 00:10:57,907
(What do you mean it's over?)

301
00:10:58,107 --> 00:11:01,477
(The next customers enter.)

302
00:11:01,917 --> 00:11:03,947
Hello. May I take your order now?

303
00:11:04,147 --> 00:11:06,817
Yes, please. Can we have three beef burger combos...

304
00:11:06,817 --> 00:11:08,857
- Yes, three beef burger combos. - and three cakes?

305
00:11:09,087 --> 00:11:10,357
- Would you like three of those? - Yes, please.

306
00:11:10,357 --> 00:11:11,357
Understood.

307
00:11:11,857 --> 00:11:14,697
Can we swap the combo drinks for ades?

308
00:11:15,027 --> 00:11:17,227
- Oh, gosh. What should we do? - It's beef.

309
00:11:17,227 --> 00:11:18,397
(The new ordering trend)

310
00:11:18,767 --> 00:11:22,337
(1 burger and 1 dessert per person)

311
00:11:22,937 --> 00:11:24,307
They ordered three carrot cakes.

312
00:11:25,037 --> 00:11:26,407
(Main Dish: 4 beef burgers, 1 shrimp burger, 1 rice cracker taco)

313
00:11:26,407 --> 00:11:27,777
(Dessert: 4 carrot cakes, 2 pomegranate ades, 2 yuzu ades)

314
00:11:28,007 --> 00:11:30,307
I'll make a glass of pomegranate ade and a glass of yuzu ade.

315
00:11:30,307 --> 00:11:31,847
- One pomegranate and one yuzu. - One more beef burger.

316
00:11:31,847 --> 00:11:34,177
(She pulls herself together and steps up to make the ades.)

317
00:11:34,617 --> 00:11:36,417
- I'll make three cakes. - Three cakes...

318
00:11:36,417 --> 00:11:37,847
- I'll make three cakes. - Okay.

319
00:11:38,547 --> 00:11:41,157
- Young Ji, we can do this. - Yes, we can.

320
00:11:41,387 --> 00:11:45,027
(She'll cook 4 beef patties at the same time.)

321
00:11:45,357 --> 00:11:50,197
(She puts her whole heart into pressing the patty.)

322
00:11:51,267 --> 00:11:52,997
The griddle is working beautifully today.

323
00:11:53,597 --> 00:11:55,067
Three beef burgers are ready...

324
00:11:55,067 --> 00:11:56,567
- for the same table. - Got it.

325
00:11:56,837 --> 00:11:57,867
- Yes, it's out. - Then...

326
00:11:57,867 --> 00:11:58,967
- let's serve the cakes too. - Okay.

327
00:11:59,207 --> 00:12:01,277
- Will you serve the cakes too? - These are for Table 12.

328
00:12:01,277 --> 00:12:02,807
- Table 12? - Yes.

329
00:12:02,807 --> 00:12:03,977
- It's perfect. - I'll go first.

330
00:12:04,037 --> 00:12:06,077
(Everything is ready for the table of 3.)

331
00:12:06,477 --> 00:12:07,977
(It feels like something is missing.)

332
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,417
- Table 12, right? I'll go. - Yes.

333
00:12:09,417 --> 00:12:12,047
- Then I'll... Oh, the shovels. - You forgot the shovels.

334
00:12:12,047 --> 00:12:13,247
(The customers almost had to peck at their food like a crane.)

335
00:12:13,487 --> 00:12:14,957
It was my first time making carrot cakes.

336
00:12:15,857 --> 00:12:16,887
Thank you.

337
00:12:16,887 --> 00:12:20,187
(With shovel spoons dug into the carrot cakes...)

338
00:12:20,457 --> 00:12:22,957
- Okay. I'll take the ticket down. - Okay.

339
00:12:24,197 --> 00:12:26,397
- Here's your food. - Thank you.

340
00:12:26,397 --> 00:12:28,867
Here are the three beef burgers you ordered.

341
00:12:28,867 --> 00:12:30,097
- Oh, no. I'm sorry. - That's okay.

342
00:12:31,167 --> 00:12:33,937
- The shrimp burger is ready. - Yes, the shrimp burger is up.

343
00:12:34,437 --> 00:12:36,107
- Two glasses of ade, and it's over. - Okay.

344
00:12:36,437 --> 00:12:37,807
(Please give me a minute.)

345
00:12:37,807 --> 00:12:39,107
- It's for Table 4. - Table 4.

346
00:12:39,107 --> 00:12:40,847
- I'll go first. - Okay.

347
00:12:42,147 --> 00:12:43,777
Thank you. I'll put it on here.

348
00:12:43,777 --> 00:12:45,147
(Kyung Soo heads out with the ade.)

349
00:12:45,387 --> 00:12:47,687
Thank you. Please enjoy. Oh, no. I'm sorry.

350
00:12:48,717 --> 00:12:49,787
It looks delicious.

351
00:12:49,787 --> 00:12:50,817
(The 1-burger-per-person table tastes the food.)

352
00:12:50,817 --> 00:12:53,627
- I can just tell it's good. - It looks amazing.

353
00:12:54,397 --> 00:12:56,857
(He finally takes his first bite of the burger.)

354
00:12:57,527 --> 00:12:58,597
This is a whole new taste.

355
00:12:59,197 --> 00:13:01,137
Indeed. Surprisingly, they go well together.

356
00:13:02,537 --> 00:13:03,537
I want to buy this recipe.

357
00:13:04,407 --> 00:13:05,437
What are you going to do with it?

358
00:13:06,937 --> 00:13:08,037
If they hire me...

359
00:13:08,037 --> 00:13:10,377
(While they talk about opening a new Space Rice Cake location...)

360
00:13:10,707 --> 00:13:12,377
- Take your time with the menu... - Yes.

361
00:13:13,147 --> 00:13:14,377
and let me know when you're ready to order.

362
00:13:14,677 --> 00:13:16,817
Anything new on the menu today?

363
00:13:17,047 --> 00:13:19,487
Yes, we're serving tacos today. It's a new menu item.

364
00:13:20,247 --> 00:13:22,457
- It's called Uno, Dos, Tres, Taco. - Can we have one of those?

365
00:13:22,457 --> 00:13:23,487
One taco.

366
00:13:24,487 --> 00:13:25,527
One taco...

367
00:13:26,087 --> 00:13:27,157
- Yes. - And...

368
00:13:27,457 --> 00:13:29,227
The taco is a hit, Mimi.

369
00:13:29,227 --> 00:13:31,127
- Is it? - The taco is selling really well.

370
00:13:31,127 --> 00:13:34,337
I owe it all to the whole team.

371
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:37,067
- One taco is ready. - One taco is ready.

372
00:13:37,067 --> 00:13:39,067
One more taco is up.

373
00:13:39,337 --> 00:13:40,807
I think it's a great idea.

374
00:13:41,777 --> 00:13:43,377
- It's good. - It's a great combination.

375
00:13:43,877 --> 00:13:45,207
(- Nice. - Is it tasty?)

376
00:13:45,507 --> 00:13:47,747
(Honestly, we think it's tasty.)

377
00:13:48,077 --> 00:13:49,117
Kyung Soo...

378
00:13:49,847 --> 00:13:51,447
- loves tacos. - That makes sense.

379
00:13:51,587 --> 00:13:54,087
(Yes. Kyung Soo, who loves tacos, came up with the recipe.)

380
00:13:54,457 --> 00:13:56,787
The taco looks pretty. I love the vibrant colors.

381
00:13:57,287 --> 00:14:00,057
(Space Rice Cake's own unique rice cracker taco)

382
00:14:00,427 --> 00:14:02,697
(But there is an obstacle.)

383
00:14:03,097 --> 00:14:05,427
One, two,

384
00:14:06,027 --> 00:14:07,737
three, four...

385
00:14:07,737 --> 00:14:08,967
(Mimi is counting rice crackers.)

386
00:14:08,967 --> 00:14:10,867
Five, six...

387
00:14:11,507 --> 00:14:13,467
And 7. It's supposed to have 7 of them, right?

388
00:14:13,467 --> 00:14:15,077
One, two, three, four, five, six, seven.

389
00:14:15,737 --> 00:14:17,277
(She's wrong.)

390
00:14:19,677 --> 00:14:21,747
Why do I get so nervous every time I count?

391
00:14:22,377 --> 00:14:23,747
- Mimi. - Yes?

392
00:14:24,047 --> 00:14:25,347
Call me when you need to count.

393
00:14:26,117 --> 00:14:27,817
One taco is up.

394
00:14:28,287 --> 00:14:32,187
(She plates 7 rice crackers for the next taco dish.)

395
00:14:32,387 --> 00:14:35,027
(Then, she tops them with the stir-fried beef.)

396
00:14:36,797 --> 00:14:37,867
There are six rice crackers there.

397
00:14:37,867 --> 00:14:38,927
(The cameraman says she has only six rice crackers.)

398
00:14:39,097 --> 00:14:41,697
You need one more rice cracker. One rice cracker is missing.

399
00:14:44,067 --> 00:14:46,437
(What? There's no way.)

400
00:14:50,037 --> 00:14:51,707
I swear, I counted right.

401
00:14:53,847 --> 00:14:55,447
(She really is missing one.)

402
00:14:56,517 --> 00:14:58,547
(She quickly adds one.)

403
00:14:59,017 --> 00:15:00,847
That was a close call.

404
00:15:01,317 --> 00:15:03,187
But I was sure I counted seven.

405
00:15:03,687 --> 00:15:05,927
I think I should go back to elementary school.

406
00:15:05,927 --> 00:15:08,327
The beef burger is up too.

407
00:15:08,427 --> 00:15:09,527
I feel bad about myself.

408
00:15:09,527 --> 00:15:10,997
(Reason for re-enrollment: Self-loathing over a rice cracker)

409
00:15:11,327 --> 00:15:12,627
- The colors are great. - Indeed.

410
00:15:12,627 --> 00:15:13,827
(The Guam Elementary School graduate did a good job despite everything.)

411
00:15:14,227 --> 00:15:18,737
(Thank you, sir.)

412
00:15:19,237 --> 00:15:20,667
Here's your food.

413
00:15:20,667 --> 00:15:21,677
(Mimi's taco made with a little help from the cameraman is served.)

414
00:15:21,677 --> 00:15:23,437
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

415
00:15:23,437 --> 00:15:24,447
(Mimi's taco made with a little help from the cameraman is served.)

416
00:15:24,447 --> 00:15:26,647
Here's the rice cracker taco you ordered.

417
00:15:27,107 --> 00:15:31,247
(How does it taste?)

418
00:15:31,817 --> 00:15:34,857
(Impressed)

419
00:15:35,287 --> 00:15:36,517
It tastes like a tortilla when you eat it.

420
00:15:37,687 --> 00:15:38,687
The moment you bite into it.

421
00:15:39,587 --> 00:15:40,687
- It's good. - Yes.

422
00:15:41,327 --> 00:15:44,527
(Fortunately, the customers give positive feedback.)

423
00:15:44,767 --> 00:15:46,827
(Right then, a group of customers finished their food.)

424
00:15:46,827 --> 00:15:48,137
- Did you enjoy the food? - Yes, we did.

425
00:15:48,137 --> 00:15:49,197
What was your favorite?

426
00:15:49,567 --> 00:15:51,567
- The shrimp burger. - The shrimp burger?

427
00:15:51,567 --> 00:15:52,707
(Everyone likes the shrimp burger.)

428
00:15:53,407 --> 00:15:55,677
- We didn't leave the food... - Oh, right.

429
00:15:55,677 --> 00:15:56,707
because it wasn't good.

430
00:15:56,707 --> 00:15:58,077
- Because you were full? - No, it was because...

431
00:15:58,647 --> 00:16:00,577
- The rice crackers vanished. - They vanished.

432
00:16:00,877 --> 00:16:02,917
- Because of the moisture... - Oh, I see.

433
00:16:02,917 --> 00:16:05,987
- The rice crackers disappeared. - They melted due to the moisture.

434
00:16:06,387 --> 00:16:09,187
- The rice crackers disappeared? - They melted away...

435
00:16:09,187 --> 00:16:10,417
- They melted from the moisture. - They melted away.

436
00:16:10,717 --> 00:16:12,427
We ended up with a lot of leftover toppings because of that.

437
00:16:12,427 --> 00:16:13,857
- Oh, no. - That...

438
00:16:14,087 --> 00:16:15,757
Thank you for your feedback. Go home safely.

439
00:16:15,757 --> 00:16:17,357
- Go home safely. - Thank you.

440
00:16:17,357 --> 00:16:18,927
- Ahk. - Goodbye.

441
00:16:18,927 --> 00:16:20,767
- Go home safely. - Goodbye.

442
00:16:20,997 --> 00:16:22,667
The rice crackers...

443
00:16:22,667 --> 00:16:23,837
(The urgent meeting about the tacos)

444
00:16:23,997 --> 00:16:27,037
- What should we do about it? - We should serve it first.

445
00:16:27,507 --> 00:16:29,137
We can't serve them separately from the toppings.

446
00:16:29,377 --> 00:16:32,447
Should we serve it with ten rice crackers?

447
00:16:32,707 --> 00:16:34,447
I guess it's the moisture from the toppings.

448
00:16:34,447 --> 00:16:35,447
(Director Doh became serious after hearing the taco feedback.)

449
00:16:35,477 --> 00:16:37,947
(Giggling)

450
00:16:38,147 --> 00:16:40,447
(Director Doh is thinking hard.)

451
00:16:42,787 --> 00:16:44,257
- Or we can do this. - Okay.

452
00:16:44,257 --> 00:16:45,687
Since the customers eat them together anyway,

453
00:16:45,687 --> 00:16:47,157
let's arrange the rice crackers around the rim of the plate...

454
00:16:47,157 --> 00:16:49,197
- and put the meat in the center. - Shall we? That's a good idea.

455
00:16:49,197 --> 00:16:50,327
(Here's Director Doh's solution.)

456
00:16:50,527 --> 00:16:54,737
(1. Serve more rice crackers and place them around the rim.)

457
00:16:54,997 --> 00:17:00,237
(2. Pile the toppings in the center.)

458
00:17:00,437 --> 00:17:02,877
(Minimizing contact with the toppings...)

459
00:17:03,137 --> 00:17:06,877
(will keep the rice crackers crunchy!)

460
00:17:07,047 --> 00:17:10,317
(Rice cracker taco version 2 is now available.)

461
00:17:10,617 --> 00:17:12,187
(Chef Mimi starts making the taco.)

462
00:17:12,387 --> 00:17:13,847
I'll try out...

463
00:17:15,187 --> 00:17:16,257
Director Doh's...

464
00:17:17,187 --> 00:17:18,457
idea.

465
00:17:18,957 --> 00:17:22,557
(Placing the rice crackers around the rim of the plate)

466
00:17:22,557 --> 00:17:23,697
Nine... Okay.

467
00:17:23,697 --> 00:17:25,427
(Placing the rice crackers around the rim of the plate)

468
00:17:25,727 --> 00:17:28,097
Just as Director Doh said,

469
00:17:28,097 --> 00:17:29,237
his way leaves the center empty.

470
00:17:29,937 --> 00:17:31,337
(Stir-fried beef)

471
00:17:31,337 --> 00:17:32,867
(Avocados)

472
00:17:32,867 --> 00:17:34,267
(Tomato salsa)

473
00:17:34,607 --> 00:17:37,107
- This is better, right? - Yes, it's way better.

474
00:17:37,837 --> 00:17:39,407
(Both Director Doh and Chef Mimi are happy with the result.)

475
00:17:39,707 --> 00:17:43,647
(Adding Parmigiano cheese that will give extra flavor...)

476
00:17:43,917 --> 00:17:46,747
(and crushed pepper)

477
00:17:46,987 --> 00:17:48,687
- This is better. - Yes, it's good.

478
00:17:48,687 --> 00:17:49,957
I did it just as you told me to.

479
00:17:50,417 --> 00:17:53,357
(The 1st plate of rice cracker taco version 2 is ready!)

480
00:17:53,627 --> 00:17:56,297
(It's done! Isn't it easy?)

481
00:17:56,297 --> 00:17:58,727
- Head Chef, I have a question. - Yes?

482
00:17:59,397 --> 00:18:00,397
Aren't you going...

483
00:18:00,397 --> 00:18:01,437
- to a Chinese restaurant later? - Yes.

484
00:18:01,437 --> 00:18:03,497
- A Chinese restaurant? - A Chinese restaurant.

485
00:18:04,237 --> 00:18:05,607
It's only a five-minute walk.

486
00:18:05,907 --> 00:18:07,467
Do you want to take a car or walk?

487
00:18:07,977 --> 00:18:09,877
But I have to...

488
00:18:09,937 --> 00:18:11,377
go home after this shift.

489
00:18:11,377 --> 00:18:13,147
- No. - But you're working in the evening.

490
00:18:13,477 --> 00:18:15,617
You said earlier that you were staying all day.

491
00:18:16,047 --> 00:18:18,387
- Come on. - Right? You're lying, aren't you?

492
00:18:18,387 --> 00:18:19,847
Kyung Soo, what are you talking about?

493
00:18:20,187 --> 00:18:22,257
Things are running smoothly right now thanks to you.

494
00:18:22,257 --> 00:18:23,457
- That's right. - Right.

495
00:18:24,087 --> 00:18:26,527
- It'll be very busy tonight. - Right.

496
00:18:27,927 --> 00:18:30,327
You should be really grateful...

497
00:18:31,397 --> 00:18:33,767
to the servers.

498
00:18:34,427 --> 00:18:36,837
(Many thoughts behind his expression)

499
00:18:36,837 --> 00:18:39,537
- Yes, I'm very grateful to them. - The servers.

500
00:18:39,837 --> 00:18:41,377
I think we only need...

501
00:18:42,207 --> 00:18:44,107
one person in the kitchen.

502
00:18:45,977 --> 00:18:48,317
(The head chef is speechless.)

503
00:18:48,447 --> 00:18:50,747
- Kyung Soo, why don't you run... - You have to work with us.

504
00:18:50,747 --> 00:18:52,117
- the kitchen by yourself tonight? - Yes.

505
00:18:52,117 --> 00:18:53,287
The four of us can serve.

506
00:18:53,947 --> 00:18:55,117
- I was just... - You're being ridiculous.

507
00:18:55,117 --> 00:18:56,387
throwing the idea out there.

508
00:18:56,957 --> 00:18:58,357
- Hello. - Hello.

509
00:18:58,357 --> 00:18:59,527
- Would you like to order? - Yes.

