00:28:25,387 --> 00:28:27,827
we'll put on a small performance for you.

773
00:28:28,557 --> 00:28:30,327
(A performance of apology)

774
00:28:30,327 --> 00:28:31,397
(Leader Lee Eun Ji, Second Kim Mi Hyun, Third Lee Young Ji,)

775
00:28:31,397 --> 00:28:32,497
(Youngest An Yu Jin, Special Guest Doh Kyung Soo)

776
00:28:32,727 --> 00:28:34,827
Five, six, seven, eight.

777
00:28:35,127 --> 00:28:36,637
(Singing)

778
00:28:36,797 --> 00:28:38,907
(An opening song nobody agreed on)

779
00:28:39,007 --> 00:28:42,407
(It's their first gig, so the members aren't used to it.)

780
00:28:43,277 --> 00:28:46,177
(The leader is in her element.)

781
00:28:46,247 --> 00:28:48,817
(A performance for one table only)

782
00:28:48,917 --> 00:28:51,677
(We sent out an unsliced pizza. Oh, my gosh.)

783
00:28:51,817 --> 00:28:54,087
(The end of the performance)

784
00:28:54,087 --> 00:28:56,257
Once again, we bow our heads...

785
00:28:56,417 --> 00:28:57,887
- in apology. - We apologize.

786
00:29:00,087 --> 00:29:01,857
Honestly, it turned out for the better.

787
00:29:01,857 --> 00:29:02,897
Thank you so much.

788
00:29:02,897 --> 00:29:04,057
- Enjoy your food. - It's 90,000 dollars' worth...

789
00:29:04,057 --> 00:29:05,197
of compensation.

790
00:29:05,397 --> 00:29:06,727
- Enjoy your food. - Excuse me,

791
00:29:06,727 --> 00:29:08,597
- Enjoy your food. - but is the pizza usually sliced?

792
00:29:08,597 --> 00:29:09,797
- Mimi. - Ours wasn't cut.

793
00:29:09,797 --> 00:29:10,937
This table too.

794
00:29:10,937 --> 00:29:12,707
Three, two, one. Let's go.

795
00:29:12,767 --> 00:29:16,077
(Quickly starting their 2nd performance)

796
00:29:16,407 --> 00:29:19,677
(There's absolute chaos.)

797
00:29:19,847 --> 00:29:22,047
(His energy is completely drained.)

798
00:29:22,277 --> 00:29:24,547
(They seem to enjoy giving their performance of apology.)

799
00:29:24,717 --> 00:29:26,687
(Hey!)

800
00:29:26,817 --> 00:29:28,617
- Once again, we bow our heads... - Thank you.

801
00:29:28,617 --> 00:29:29,787
- in apology. - We apologize.

802
00:29:29,787 --> 00:29:31,457
- We're very sorry. - We apologize.

803
00:29:31,457 --> 00:29:32,657
(The group performance tour comes to an end.)

804
00:29:32,657 --> 00:29:33,657
We apologize.

805
00:29:34,657 --> 00:29:35,997
I just asked out of curiosity.

806
00:29:35,997 --> 00:29:38,197
I didn't know what the problem was.

807
00:29:39,027 --> 00:29:40,227
Look how we cut it.

808
00:29:40,227 --> 00:29:41,527
(The pizza still looks ridiculous.)

809
00:29:41,527 --> 00:29:42,767
That was amazing.

810
00:29:42,767 --> 00:29:43,867
I wonder...

811
00:29:43,867 --> 00:29:45,407
who's in charge of the pizza.

812
00:29:46,207 --> 00:29:47,807
I'm actually grateful.

813
00:29:47,867 --> 00:29:49,307
(They even got to enjoy a live show.)

814
00:29:49,307 --> 00:29:51,537
- It's 100,000 dollars' worth. - I know.

815
00:29:52,247 --> 00:29:55,047
- It's more than 100,000 dollars. - Exactly.

816
00:29:55,417 --> 00:29:58,717
Gosh, our lunch service is finally over.

817
00:29:58,717 --> 00:30:00,617
- Well done, everyone. - Oh, my.

818
00:30:00,947 --> 00:30:02,017
I'm okay.

819
00:30:02,187 --> 00:30:04,357
- But you don't look okay at all. - I'm really okay.

820
00:30:05,327 --> 00:30:08,157
(She's too exhausted to even stand.)

821
00:30:08,327 --> 00:30:10,057
Let's have something to drink.

822
00:30:10,657 --> 00:30:12,567
(Refreshing and fizzy)

823
00:30:12,767 --> 00:30:14,497
(Quenching their thirst with a sweet drink)

824
00:30:14,497 --> 00:30:16,097
It hits the spot when you're exhausted.

825
00:30:17,937 --> 00:30:19,267
- What do you think, Mimi? - It's very refreshing.

826
00:30:19,437 --> 00:30:21,807
I can enjoy every last drop of it.

827
00:30:24,007 --> 00:30:25,137
This is the best.

828
00:30:25,647 --> 00:30:27,077
(Drinking)

829
00:30:27,747 --> 00:30:30,377
(Bubbly and refreshing just like Yu Jin)

830
00:30:30,477 --> 00:30:33,047
It'd go really well...

831
00:30:33,047 --> 00:30:34,847
- It'd be a perfect match. - with slightly greasy food.

832
00:30:35,657 --> 00:30:38,417
It's 30 percent lower in sugar and calories.

833
00:30:38,417 --> 00:30:40,457
- That's great. - That explains it.

834
00:30:40,657 --> 00:30:43,457
(After enjoying a sweet break)

835
00:30:43,697 --> 00:30:44,857
I'm curious about this too.

836
00:30:44,857 --> 00:30:46,227
Don't look. I'll tell you over there.

837
00:30:46,627 --> 00:30:47,697
Go back to your seat.

838
00:30:47,697 --> 00:30:50,637
(It's time to tally up the sales again.)

839
00:30:51,297 --> 00:30:53,067
- I'll announce the results. - Five hundred?

840
00:30:53,267 --> 00:30:54,537
Do you have any guesses?

841
00:30:54,537 --> 00:30:55,607
How about 550 dollars?

842
00:30:56,137 --> 00:30:57,237
I think it's 600 dollars.

843
00:30:57,377 --> 00:30:58,437
(How about you?)

844
00:30:58,607 --> 00:30:59,607
Is it 570 dollars?

845
00:30:59,607 --> 00:31:01,577
We didn't have many customers today. How about 400 dollars?

846
00:31:02,777 --> 00:31:04,077
(Drumroll, please.)

847
00:31:04,077 --> 00:31:05,117
(Getting the crowd hyped up)

848
00:31:05,317 --> 00:31:09,257
(How much did they make during lunch?)

849
00:31:09,417 --> 00:31:11,057
We made 1,050 dollars.

850
00:31:12,887 --> 00:31:14,427
How did we earn so much?

851
00:31:14,527 --> 00:31:16,057
We sold so many pizzas.

852
00:31:16,397 --> 00:31:17,497
We said we were sold out,

853
00:31:17,497 --> 00:31:19,197
but we still made more dough and sold more pizzas.

854
00:31:19,497 --> 00:31:21,127
Well done.

855
00:31:21,127 --> 00:31:22,367
- We did an awesome job. - We made 1,000 dollars.

856
00:31:22,697 --> 00:31:24,067
We made 1,050 dollars.

857
00:31:24,567 --> 00:31:25,737
That's incredible.

858
00:31:25,937 --> 00:31:29,407
(The applause just keeps coming.)

859
00:31:29,637 --> 00:31:30,807
How did this happen?

860
00:31:30,977 --> 00:31:32,477
Kyung Soo, well done.

861
00:31:32,807 --> 00:31:34,147
(It's my pleasure.)

862
00:31:34,507 --> 00:31:36,177
Did you pay for your drink?

863
00:31:36,647 --> 00:31:38,117
(The head chef chimes in with a complaint.)

864
00:31:38,117 --> 00:31:39,147
I guess you didn't.

865
00:31:39,547 --> 00:31:40,747
How much is it?

866
00:31:40,917 --> 00:31:41,947
It's two dollars.

867
00:31:41,947 --> 00:31:42,957
- It's two dollars. - Okay.

868
00:31:42,957 --> 00:31:45,957
Two dollars and the bun that you ruined earlier.

869
00:31:46,457 --> 00:31:47,487
What else?

870
00:31:47,487 --> 00:31:48,557
- Did he ruin a bun too? - What else?

871
00:31:48,557 --> 00:31:49,797
He burnt a piece of dough.

872
00:31:49,797 --> 00:31:50,897
How much is that?

873
00:31:50,997 --> 00:31:52,167
- Hey, listen. - What?

874
00:31:52,167 --> 00:31:53,327
Let's not be too hard on Kyung Soo.

875
00:31:53,327 --> 00:31:56,267
- This guide to taking orders... - Why?

876
00:31:56,867 --> 00:31:58,867
that Kyung Soo wrote himself...

877
00:31:59,037 --> 00:32:01,237
- at the counter is very touching. - What is it?

878
00:32:01,237 --> 00:32:03,307
It makes me feel sad...

879
00:32:03,677 --> 00:32:05,207
and incredibly grateful.

880
00:32:05,947 --> 00:32:07,707
"As spicy as Buldak."

881
00:32:09,017 --> 00:32:10,177
(Just in case the customer can't handle the spices...)

882
00:32:10,177 --> 00:32:12,947
Kyung Soo wrote it all down.

883
00:32:12,947 --> 00:32:14,387
(He carefully noted it down.)

884
00:32:15,887 --> 00:32:18,617
It breaks my heart to see something like this.

885
00:32:19,227 --> 00:32:20,587
If he helps out tonight,

886
00:32:20,587 --> 00:32:22,157
should we increase his hourly wage?

887
00:32:22,157 --> 00:32:23,397
Pay him more?

888
00:32:23,557 --> 00:32:26,597
- How would you feel about that? - Do you have a rate in mind?

889
00:32:27,297 --> 00:32:29,637
So far, I worked 4 hours... Did I work 3 hours?

890
00:32:29,767 --> 00:32:31,037
- Because... - In the morning,

891
00:32:31,037 --> 00:32:32,237
he started at 9:30am.

892
00:32:32,237 --> 00:32:34,837
- But he was our instructor then. - From 9:30am?

893
00:32:34,937 --> 00:32:36,907
- From 9:30am. - I prepared the tacos this morning.

894
00:32:36,907 --> 00:32:38,237
- Really? - We should count his hours...

895
00:32:38,237 --> 00:32:39,547
starting at 9:30am.

896
00:32:39,547 --> 00:32:41,947
- From 9:30am to 3:30pm, - Right.

897
00:32:41,947 --> 00:32:43,277
- he worked six hours. - Yes.

898
00:32:43,277 --> 00:32:46,217
He'll work from 5pm to 9pm, so that's 4 hours.

899
00:32:46,217 --> 00:32:47,817
- The total is ten hours. My gosh. - Yes.

900
00:32:48,387 --> 00:32:50,517
Then let's make it two dollars per hour.

901
00:32:50,917 --> 00:32:52,427
Two dollars per hour?

902
00:32:53,527 --> 00:32:54,887
How about ten dollars? Let's be generous.

903
00:32:55,727 --> 00:32:57,057
I was going to start at 20 dollars.

904
00:32:57,057 --> 00:32:58,597
- Twenty dollars? - Twenty dollars?

905
00:32:59,027 --> 00:33:00,927
Then we have to pay the part-timer 200 dollars.

906
00:33:00,927 --> 00:33:03,497
No way. We won't be able to buy SK Hynix stock.

907
00:33:04,097 --> 00:33:06,237
What if we pay him 200 dollars...

908
00:33:06,237 --> 00:33:07,837
and have him work...

909
00:33:07,837 --> 00:33:09,307
on the second floor all night?

910
00:33:09,307 --> 00:33:10,537
Make him work nonstop?

911
00:33:10,637 --> 00:33:12,607
- I'm sorry. - We can get our money's worth.

912
00:33:12,607 --> 00:33:13,647
- That sounds good. - I'm sorry.

913
00:33:13,977 --> 00:33:15,647
- Let's pay him 200 dollars. - Right.

914
00:33:16,077 --> 00:33:17,577
- For one day... - We can ask him...

915
00:33:17,577 --> 00:33:19,947
- to make dough nonstop. - That sounds good.

916
00:33:19,947 --> 00:33:22,317
If we make 2,000 dollars in sales tonight,

917
00:33:22,317 --> 00:33:24,317
paying him 200 dollars will be worth it.

918
00:33:24,557 --> 00:33:25,987
That's a great deal for us.

919
00:33:26,127 --> 00:33:27,387
Let's give him 250 dollars...

920
00:33:27,387 --> 00:33:28,897
and make him work all night going up and down.

921
00:33:29,197 --> 00:33:31,997
We'll make him prepare 30 pieces of dough.

922
00:33:31,997 --> 00:33:33,967
If he makes dough and works on the second floor,

923
00:33:33,967 --> 00:33:35,097
paying him 200 dollars...

924
00:33:35,097 --> 00:33:36,637
We'll be really generous...

925
00:33:36,637 --> 00:33:37,737
and pay you 250 dollars.

926
00:33:38,237 --> 00:33:40,467
Did you say 250 dollars? Okay.

927
00:33:40,667 --> 00:33:43,237
(Wage negotiations are done.)

928
00:33:43,637 --> 00:33:44,977
Is there a contract?

929
00:33:45,477 --> 00:33:47,507
There's a clause that I want to add.

930
00:33:48,077 --> 00:33:49,817
Can I read the clauses before I sign?

931
00:33:49,817 --> 00:33:50,817
Of course.

932
00:33:50,817 --> 00:33:52,287
If I don't like what I see,

933
00:33:52,287 --> 00:33:53,647
- can I just go home? - Of course.

934
00:33:53,647 --> 00:33:54,817
- You can't go home. - Really?

935
00:33:54,817 --> 00:33:56,217
- You can't go home. - She said, "Of course."

936
00:33:56,217 --> 00:33:58,217
You were employed by the HQ,

937
00:33:58,217 --> 00:34:00,427
- Right. - so that's a separate matter.

938
00:34:00,657 --> 00:34:01,787
(Something feels fishy.)

939
00:34:01,787 --> 00:34:02,857
Please wait. They're in the pantry.

940
00:34:02,857 --> 00:34:05,397
Can you tell me what you want?

941
00:34:05,397 --> 00:34:07,967
I'd like him to serve on the second floor.

942
00:34:08,197 --> 00:34:10,197
- That's what... - We shouldn't add that.

943
00:34:10,197 --> 00:34:12,037
- We can take care of that... - What do you want him to do?

944
00:34:12,037 --> 00:34:13,837
I want him to make 30 pieces of dough.

945
00:34:13,837 --> 00:34:16,477
- Okay, write that down. - That sounds good.

946
00:34:16,477 --> 00:34:17,777
- All right. - It's a contract.

947
00:34:17,777 --> 00:34:19,947
And frying tater tots.

948
00:34:20,047 --> 00:34:21,877
(An awkward chuckle)

949
00:34:22,047 --> 00:34:23,947
I'd like him to check if the pizzas are sliced.

950
00:34:23,947 --> 00:34:25,417
- You should do that instead. - It should be checked.

951
00:34:25,417 --> 00:34:27,547
- You should do it. - You do it, Mimi.

952
00:34:27,547 --> 00:34:29,157
- But I... - You can do it yourself.

953
00:34:29,157 --> 00:34:31,087
I have no memory. I'm sorry.

954
00:34:31,087 --> 00:34:33,257
(The contract drafting begins.)

955
00:34:33,557 --> 00:34:35,327
- We can write about the dough. - Minimum 30.

956
00:34:35,327 --> 00:34:36,327
He has to make dough.

957
00:34:36,327 --> 00:34:38,857
Making a minimum of 30 to a maximum of 40.

958
00:34:39,267 --> 00:34:40,297
Let's do that.

959
00:34:40,297 --> 00:34:41,397
(Whispering)

960
00:34:41,397 --> 00:34:43,497
From 30... No, like this.

961
00:34:43,497 --> 00:34:44,537
- Minimum? - Like this.

962
00:34:44,537 --> 00:34:45,637
Right.

963
00:34:46,107 --> 00:34:48,107
Hurry up and give it to me. What are you guys doing?

964
00:34:48,737 --> 00:34:52,347
- Just... - Just say that it's a requirement.

965
00:34:53,147 --> 00:34:55,047
- It's done. - Okay.

966
00:34:55,047 --> 00:34:57,847
(The contract is completed.)

967
00:34:58,047 --> 00:35:01,317
(All he has to do is sign it.)

968
00:35:01,317 --> 00:35:02,587
The payment is 250 dollars.

969
00:35:03,487 --> 00:35:07,987
(At first glance, it looks like an ordinary contract.)

970
00:35:07,987 --> 00:35:09,357
"Pizza dough..."

971
00:35:09,997 --> 00:35:11,627
How many is it? Is it 30 or 40?

972
00:35:11,627 --> 00:35:13,827
- Minimum 30. - Minimum 30.

973
00:35:14,097 --> 00:35:15,367
Maximum 40.

974
00:35:15,767 --> 00:35:18,397
(Something still feels off.)

975
00:35:18,637 --> 00:35:21,337
(Hurry up and sign it.)

976
00:35:21,337 --> 00:35:22,407
Thirty?

977
00:35:23,237 --> 00:35:25,337
- Okay. - We'll help you out.

978
00:35:25,337 --> 00:35:27,377
- You won't be making 40 yourself. - Of course not.

979
00:35:27,377 --> 00:35:29,577
We're doing it together. Got it?

980
00:35:30,717 --> 00:35:32,687
- He signed it. - He did it.

981
00:35:32,947 --> 00:35:34,147
Yes!

982
00:35:34,147 --> 00:35:36,287
(The deal with Doh Kyung Soo is official.)

983
00:35:36,517 --> 00:35:37,817
Did you read it carefully?

984
00:35:37,817 --> 00:35:39,357
I don't think he read the bottom part.

985
00:35:39,357 --> 00:35:40,387
What?

986
00:35:40,387 --> 00:35:42,187
- It's nothing. - It's nothing.

987
00:35:42,187 --> 00:35:43,557
- It's okay. - Everything was written on it.

988
00:35:43,557 --> 00:35:44,827
- It was written on it. - It's nothing.

989
00:35:44,957 --> 00:35:47,127
- Thirty or forty... - Thank you so much.

990
00:35:47,127 --> 00:35:48,167
- Thank you. - Thank you.

991
00:35:48,167 --> 00:35:49,197
Honesty.

992
00:35:49,197 --> 00:35:50,237
- Humility. - Humility.

993
00:35:50,237 --> 00:35:51,537
- Ahk. - Ahk.

994
00:35:51,537 --> 00:35:53,367
- Take a break. - Take a break.

995
00:35:53,367 --> 00:35:54,467
Let's go and eat.

996
00:35:54,737 --> 00:35:58,607
(The truth is...)

997
00:35:58,607 --> 00:36:00,177
(A secret toxic clause was hidden inside.)

998
00:36:00,177 --> 00:36:01,507
(Unlimited serving on the 2nd floor)

999
00:36:01,677 --> 00:36:05,077
(He tries to look over the contract again.)

1000
00:36:05,077 --> 00:36:07,187
Right. What did you write?

1001
00:36:07,187 --> 00:36:08,217
It's nothing.

1002
00:36:08,317 --> 00:36:09,787
Thirty to forty dough pieces.

1003
00:36:10,357 --> 00:36:11,517
We did a good job writing it, right?

1004
00:36:11,517 --> 00:36:13,587
(He can't help but feel like he's been played.)

1005
00:36:13,587 --> 00:36:15,457
- He has no idea. - Well done.

1006
00:36:16,527 --> 00:36:17,897
Hide it somewhere far away.

1007
00:36:19,467 --> 00:36:21,327
He couldn't see it because I was holding it like this.

1008
00:36:21,327 --> 00:36:22,327
I thought so.

1009
00:36:22,367 --> 00:36:24,937
(It's time for lunch!)

1010
00:36:24,937 --> 00:36:26,137
We can all share it.

1011
00:36:26,137 --> 00:36:27,707
Stir-fried jjajangmyeon and jjamppong.

1012
00:36:27,707 --> 00:36:29,007
Since you're making 250 dollars today,

1013
00:36:29,007 --> 00:36:30,377
- eat as much as you want. - Eat a lot.

1014
00:36:30,377 --> 00:36:31,377
- Okay. - Eat a lot.

1015
00:36:31,377 --> 00:36:32,707
Did you promise to pay him 250 dollars?

1016
00:36:32,707 --> 00:36:33,907
Yes, for today's work.

1017
00:36:34,207 --> 00:36:36,077
- We gave him a lot of work. - We wrote a contract.

1018
00:36:36,077 --> 00:36:37,717
They told me to make 30 pieces of dough.

1019
00:36:37,717 --> 00:36:38,947
- Actually, it's 40. - It's 40.

1020
00:36:38,947 --> 00:36:40,017
From 30 to 40.

1021
00:36:40,017 --> 00:36:41,217
- Right. - Maximum of 40.

1022
00:36:41,217 --> 00:36:43,717
(The Earth Arcaders are strict about their contract.)

1023
00:36:44,357 --> 00:36:45,827
Shouldn't we get tangsuyuk?

1024
00:36:45,987 --> 00:36:47,087
We ordered it.

1025
00:36:47,157 --> 00:36:48,227
- And chili shrimp. - And chili shrimp.

1026
00:36:48,227 --> 00:36:49,457
You can order whatever you want.

1027
00:36:49,457 --> 00:36:51,027
You should eat more. Eat a lot.

1028
00:36:51,257 --> 00:36:52,697
You'll be doing a tough job later.

1029
00:36:53,267 --> 00:36:55,327
He'll be doing a tough job later?

1030
00:36:55,497 --> 00:36:56,797
(For tough labor in the evening,)

1031
00:36:56,797 --> 00:36:58,037
(he makes his choice carefully.)

1032
